                  %mo ↪
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \hookrightarrow A
            is naturally a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            under inclusion of subalgebras.
          %h3#as_a_site_for_noncommutative_geometry As a site for noncommutative geometry
          %p
            Various authors have proposed (
            %a{:href => "#ButterfieldHamiltonIsham"}> Butterfield-Hamilton-Isham
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#DoeringIsham"} Döring-Isham
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#HeunenLandsmanSpitters"} Heunen-Landsmann-Spitters
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star+algebra"} C-star algebra
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+geometry"} noncommutative geometry
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} formal dual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(A)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            may be understood as a commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}_A
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ComSub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ComSub(A)
            or its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ComSub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ComSub(A)^{op}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+locale"} compact
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+locale"} regular locale
          %h3#as_a_site_for_noncommutative_phase_spaces As a site for noncommutative phase spaces
          %p
            Specifically, consider the case that the algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℋ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = B(\mathcal{H})
            is that of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+operator"} bounded operator
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+quantum+observables"} algebra of quantum observables
            and the commutative subalgebras are then “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+contexts"}> classical contexts
            ”.
          %p
            Applying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bohrification"} Bohrification
            to this situation (see there for more discussion), one finds that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(A)
            internal to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}_A
            behaves like the noncommutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            of a system of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+algebra"} operator algebra
            then have geometric analogs in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒯
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}_A
          %p
            Notably the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kochen-Specker+theorem"} Kochen-Specker theorem
            says that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(B(\mathcal{H}))
            = succeed "s/no" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} global element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ComSub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ComSub(A)
            in the first place in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#ButterfieldIsham"} ButterfieldIsham
          %p
            Moreover, inside
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}_A
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanical
            kinematics encoded by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℋ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(\mathcal{H})
            looks like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mechanics"} classical mechanics
            kinematics internal to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}_A
            (
            %a{:href => "#HeunenLandsmanSpitters"}> HeunenLandsmannSpitters
            , following
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#DoeringIsham"} DöringIsham
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(A)
                are identified with the quantum
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state"} state
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting algebra
                of quantum logic.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable"}> observable
                s are morphisms of internal
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi IR
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(A) \to IR
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi IR
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} IR
                is the
                = succeed "." do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    interval domain
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/interval+domain"} ?
          %p
            The assignment to a noncommutative algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %munder
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo ̲
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underline{\Sigma}_A
            internal to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}_A
            has been called
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bohrification"} Bohrification
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nils+Bohr"} Nils Bohr
            whose heuristic writings about the nature of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            as being probed by classical (= commutative) context one may argue is being formalized by this construction.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general_2 General
          .num_lemma
            %h6#observation Observation
            %p
              The poset of commutative subalgebras
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(A)
              is always an (unbounded) meet-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semilattice"}> semilattice
              \. If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              itself is commutative then it is a bounded meet semilattice, with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              itself being the top element.
          %h3#RelationToJordanAlgebras Relation to Jordan algebras
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_J
            for its corresponding
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jordan+algebra"} Jordan algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi J
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi J
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \circ : A_J \otimes A_J \to A_J
            is the symmetrization of the product in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mi b
                    %mo +
                    %mi b
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \circ b = \frac{1}{2}(a b + b a)
          .num_lemma
            %h6#observation_2 Observation
            %p
              There exist von Neumann algebras
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              such that there exists a Jordan algebra isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_J \to B_J
              but not an algebra isomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p By
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"}> Alain Connes
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A factor not anti-isomorphic to itself
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1970940"} JSTOR
            %p
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/von+Neumann+algebra+factor"} von Neumann algebra factor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              with no algebra isomorphism to its opposite algebra
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{op}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi J
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi op
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_J \simeq (A^{op})_J
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, B
              be
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/von+Neumann+algebra"} von Neumann algebra
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_2
              = succeed "-summand" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/von+Neumann+algebra+factor"} von Neumann algebra factor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ComSub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ComSub(A)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ComSub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ComSub(B)
              be their posets of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+C-star-algebra"} commutative
              sub-von Neumann algebras.
            %p
              Then every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ComSub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ComSub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ComSub(A) \to ComSub(B)
              of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jordan+algebra"} Jordan algebra
              isomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi J
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_J \to B_J
          %p
            This is the theorem in (
            %a{:href => "#HardingDoering"}> Harding-Döring
            ).
          %p
            There is a generalization of this theorem to more general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star+algebras"} C-star algebras
            in (
            %a{:href => "#Hamhalter"}> Hamhalter
            ).
          %p
            For more on this see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Harding-D%C3%B6ring-Hamhalter+theorem"} Harding-Döring-Hamhalter theorem
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              This is related to the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alfsen-Shultz+theorem"} Alfsen-Shultz theorem
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state+on+an+operator+algebra"} states
              precisely if they are Jordan-isomorphic.
          %h3#the_presheaf_topos_over_
            The presheaf topos over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ComSub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ComSub(A)^{op}
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star+algebra"} C-star algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ComSub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ComSub(A)
              for its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
              of sub-
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              \-algebras. Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒯
                      %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ComSub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{T}_A := [ComSub(A),Set]
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ComSub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ComSub(A)^{op}
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bohr+topos"} Bohr topos
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              This opposite order on commutative subalgebras may be seen as the information order from
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kripke+semantics"} Kripke semantics
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ComSub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ComSub(A)
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#DoeringIsham"} Döring-Isham 07
              %em coarse-graining semantics
              of quantum mechanics. See also at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+presheaf"} spectral presheaf
          .num_lemma
            %h6#observation_3 Observation
            %p
              The topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒯
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}_A
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+topos"} localic topos
          %p
            Because
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ComSub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ComSub(A)
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posite"} posite
          %h3#the_locale_
            The locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(A)
          #JordanIsosAndCSubIsos.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒯
                      %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\mathbb{A} : B \mapsto U(B)) \;\; \in \mathcal{T}_A
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(B)
              is the underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              of the commutative subalgebra
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒯
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}_A
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#HeunenLandsmanSpitters"}> HeunenLandsmanSpitters, theorem 5
            ).
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+Gelfand+duality+theorem"} constructive Gelfand duality theorem
              there is uniquely a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(A)
              internal to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒯
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}_A
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔸
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}
              is the internal commutative
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(A)
          %p
            This observation is amplified in (
            %a{:href => "#HeunenLandsmanSpitters"}> HeunenLandsmanSpitters
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \mathcal{B}(H)
              is the algebra of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+operator"} bounded operator
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gt 2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kochen-Specker+theorem"} Kochen-Specker theorem
              implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(A)
              has no points/no
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} global element
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#HeunenLandsmanSpitters"}> HeunenLandsmanSpitters, theorem 6
            ), following (
            %a{:href => "#ButterfieldHamiltonIsham"}> Butterfield-Hamilton-Isham
            ).
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general_3 General
          %p
            The proposal that the the noncommutative geometry of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is fruitfully studied via the commutative geometry over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ComSub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ComSub(A)
            goes back to
          %ul
            %li#ButterfieldHamiltonIsham
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeremy+Butterfield"}> Jeremy Butterfield
                , John Hamilton,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Isham"} Chris Isham
                %em A topos perspective on the Kochen-Specker theorem
              %p
                %em I. quantum states as generalized valuations
                International Journal of Theoretical Physics, 37(11):2669–2733, 1998.
              %p
                %em II. conceptual aspects and classical analogues
                International Journal of Theoretical Physics, 38(3):827–859, 1999
              %p
                %em III. Von Neumann algebras as the base category
                International Journal of Theoretical Physics, 39(6):1413–1436, 2000.
          %p
            The proposal that the non-commutativity of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            is fruitfully understood in the light of this has been amplified in a series of articles
          %ul
            %li#DoeringIsham
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+D%C3%B6ring"}> Andreas Döring
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Isham"} Chris Isham
              %em A topos foundation for theories of physics
              Journal of Mathematical Physics (2008)
          %p
            The presheaf topos on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ComSub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ComSub(A)^{op}
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bohr+topos"}> Bohr topos
            ) and its internal localic Gelfand dual to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#HeunenLandsmanSpitters
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Heunen"}> Chris Heunen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaas+Landsman"} Klaas Landsman
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bas+Spitters"} Bas Spitters
              %em A topos for algebraic quantum theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0709.4364"}> arXiv:0709.4364
              )
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory+and+physics"} higher category theory and physics
          %h3#ReferencesRelationToJordanAlgebras Relation to Jordan algebras
          %p
            The
            %a{:href => "#RelationToJordanAlgebras"} relation to Jordan algebras
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ComSub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ComSub(A)
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#HardingDoering
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Harding"}> John Harding
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+D%C3%B6ring"} Andreas Döring
              %em Abelian subalgebras and the Jordan structure of a von Neumann algebra
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1009.4945"}> arXiv:1009.4945
              )
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/von+Neumann+algebra"} von Neumann algebra
            and more generally for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebra"} C*-algebra
            in
          %ul
            %li#Hamhalter
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Hamhalter"}> Jan Hamhalter
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Isomorphisms of ordered structures of abelian
                  = succeed "-subalgebras" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
                  = succeed "-algebras" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.jmaa.2011.05.035"} 10.1016/j.jmaa.2011.05.035
          %p
            See at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Harding-D%C3%B6ring-Hamhalter+theorem"} Harding-Döring-Hamhalter theorem
        .revisedby
